note.text:
Triangles named by their sides:
• equilateral: three equal sides; its three angles are equal, each 60°;
• isosceles: two equal sides; the two base angles are equal;
• scalene: no equal sides.
A right-angled triangle has one angle of 90°; the side opposite the right angle is the hypotenuse (the longest side). A triangle can be right-angled and isosceles (angles 90°, 45°, 45°).
